.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd September 25, 2026
.Dt RC.SUBR 8
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm rc.subr
.Nd functions for rc.d scripts
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Li .\& /etc/rc.subr
.Pp
.Nm checkyesno Ar var
.Nm check_pidfile Ar pidfile procname
.Nm check_process Ar procname
.Nm debug Ar message
.Nm err Ar exitval message
.Nm force_depend Ar script Op Ar var
.Nm info Ar message
.Nm load_rc_config Op Ar name
.Nm run_rc_command Ar command Op Ar argument ...
.Nm wait_for_pids Ar pid ...
.Nm warn Ar message
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The functions of
.Fx Ns 's
.Nm
are built into
.Xr init_sh 8 ,
so that
.Xr rc 8
scripts written for it run unchanged.
.Li .\& /etc/rc.subr
is accepted and has no effect in
.Xr init_sh 8 ;
a script started by any other shell re-runs itself under
.Xr init_sh 8 .
.Pp
A typical script:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
#!/sbin/init_sh
#
# PROVIDE: food
# REQUIRE: DAEMON
# KEYWORD: shutdown

\&. /etc/rc.subr

name="food"
rcvar="food_enable"
command="/usr/sbin/food"
pidfile="/var/run/food.pid"

load_rc_config $name
run_rc_command "$1"
.Ed
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Ic checkyesno Ar var
Exit 0 if the variable
.Ar var
is
.Dq YES ,
.Dq TRUE ,
.Dq ON
or
.Dq 1 ,
and 1 if it is
.Dq NO ,
.Dq FALSE ,
.Dq OFF
or
.Dq 0 ,
in any case.
Any other value is reported and counts as no.
.It Ic check_pidfile Ar pidfile procname
Print the process ID in
.Ar pidfile
if that process exists and is running
.Ar procname .
.It Ic check_process Ar procname
Print the IDs of the processes running
.Ar procname .
.It Ic debug Ar message
Print
.Ar message
on the standard error if
.Va rc_debug
is enabled.
.It Ic err Ar exitval message
Print
.Ar message
on the standard error and exit with status
.Ar exitval .
.It Ic force_depend Ar script
Start the service
.Pa /etc/rc.d/ Ns Ar script
if it is not running, whether or not it is enabled.
.It Ic info Ar message
Print
.Ar message
if
.Va rc_info
is enabled.
.It Ic load_rc_config Op Ar name
Load
.Pa /etc/defaults/rc.conf
and the files in
.Va rc_conf_files ,
once, and then
.Pa /etc/rc.conf.d/ Ns Ar name
if it exists.
The files are read, not run: see
.Xr rc.conf 5 .
.It Ic run_rc_command Ar command Op Ar argument ...
Carry out
.Ar command ,
as described in
.Xr rc 8 ,
using the variables below.
.It Ic wait_for_pids Ar pid ...
Wait until the processes have exited.
.It Ic warn Ar message
Print
.Ar message
on the standard error.
.El
.Pp
.Ic run_rc_command
uses these variables:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Va name
The service's name.
Required.
.It Va rcvar
The
.Xr rc.conf 5
variable enabling the service.
If empty, the service is always enabled.
.It Va command
The program to start, followed by
.Va ${name}_flags
from
.Xr rc.conf 5
(or
.Va flags )
and
.Va command_args .
.Va ${name}_program
overrides it.
.It Va pidfile
The file holding the running service's process ID.
.It Va procname
The program name that identifies the running service; defaults to
.Va command .
.It Va sig_stop
The signal that stops the service; default
.Dv TERM .
.It Va extra_commands
Commands besides the standard ones.
.It Va required_dirs , required_files
Must exist for the service to start.
.It Va ${command}_cmd
Replaces the built-in handling of
.Ar command .
.It Va ${command}_precmd , ${command}_postcmd
Run before and after
.Ar command .
A failing
.Va _precmd
stops the command.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr rc.conf 5 ,
.Xr init_sh 8 ,
.Xr rc 8 ,
.Xr rcorder 8
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
first appeared in
.Nx 1.3 .
These built-ins were written for OxideBSD.
.Sh BUGS
.Va ${name}_user
is not supported yet.
